        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>Cyril reads the opening &#x27;biblos geneseōs Iēsou Christou&#x27; as a deliberate echo of the Septuagintal &#x27;biblos geneseōs anthrōpōn&#x27; (Gen 5:1): the lineage of the First Adam and the lineage of the Last Adam stand in typological mirror. The Davidic-Solomonic descent is not biological boast but covenantal fulfillment — the Son who is by nature the Father&#x27;s only-begotten is by economy the prophesied Son of David. Tewahedo Kǝbrä Nägäśt&#x27;s Solomonic-dynastic theology reads its own Davidic claim through this Matthean lens.</p></aside>',
