        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On the conception &#x27;of the Holy Spirit&#x27;: Cyril is exact — the Spirit is divine cause, not divine progenitor; the Word himself takes flesh of the Theotokos by the Spirit&#x27;s overshadowing. The virginity of Mary in conception, parturition, and after is preserved entire, because the One conceived is the Maker of nature, not its captive. Tewahedo Wǝddase Maryam preserves this Cyrillian language precisely in its Monday-cycle praises.</p></aside>',
