        "d",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The Trinitarian theophany at the Jordan: the Father&#x27;s voice from heaven, the Son in the river, the Spirit as dove. Cyril names this the most pellucid Trinitarian moment of the Gospels; the three persons disclose themselves discretely without confusion. Tewahedo Geʿez baptismal anaphoras cite Mt 3:16-17 alongside Lk 3:21-22 as the canonical Trinitarian baptismal locus.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
