        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>On the wilderness temptation: Cyril reads Christ as the New Adam who wins where the First Adam fell. Bread-test (flesh), kingdom-test (world), pinnacle-test (presumption) recapitulate and reverse the tripartite ancient defeat. Tewahedo Hudadē (Great Lent), forty days of fasting through Holy Week, is patterned on this wilderness victory.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
