        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;And he opened his mouth and taught them&#x27; — Cyril marvels that the phrase is otherwise reserved for solemn prophetic utterance (Acts 8:35, 10:34). The mouth that speaks here is the same Logos that spoke creation; the Sermon is the new-creation parallel to Gen 1&#x27;s &#x27;God said&#x27;.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
