        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Blessed are the meek; for they shall inherit the earth&#x27; — Cyril sees the fulfillment of Ps 37:11 (LXX 36:11) precisely here. The praeis are not the spineless but the non-grasping; they inherit precisely because they do not seize. Tewahedo monastic non-violence (the &#x27;absent sword&#x27; tradition) anchors here.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
