        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Blessed are they which are persecuted for righteousness&#x27; sake&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s martyric-makarism text. The dia dikaiosynēn qualifier is crucial — persecution as such is not blessed, only persecution for the right cause. Tewahedo Sämā&#x27;ǝtāt cycle reads Mt 5:10 alongside Acts 7 as the martyric charter.</p></aside>',
