        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Blessed are ye, when men shall revile you and persecute you… for my sake&#x27; — Cyril moves from the third-person makarismos to the direct second-person address: the disciples themselves are now the target. The shift signals the eschatological transition from ancient martyrology to specifically Christ-witness martyrdom.</p></aside>',
