        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Rejoice and be exceeding glad; for so persecuted they the prophets which were before you&#x27; — Cyril joins the New-Covenant martyrs to the Old prophets in single line of witness. The chairete kai agalliasthē is imperative joy, not optional emotion. Tewahedo liturgy preserves this exultant-martyr posture in the Mahǝlet chants for martyrs&#x27; feasts.</p></aside>',
