        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Ye are the salt of the earth&#x27; — Cyril reads the salt-image as both preservative (against the world&#x27;s corruption) and seasoning (making creation savor itself). Mōranthē (lose savor) is the believers&#x27; worst danger: the only worse fate than persecution is irrelevance.</p></aside>',
