        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Ye are the light of the world&#x27; — Cyril marks the dual claim. Christ elsewhere claims this for himself (Jn 8:12); here he confers it on the Church derivatively. The polis epi orous (city on a hill) is the visible Church — concealment of holy life is impossible by design.</p></aside>',
