        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Neither do men light a candle, and put it under a bushel&#x27; — Cyril takes the lampstand image to argue against esoteric Christianity. The Gospel is public-by-essence; the modion (bushel) is rebuked because it hides what must shine. Tewahedo public-procession liturgy (Tǝmqät outdoor mass) embodies this principle.</p></aside>',
