        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Whosoever therefore shall break one of these least commandments… shall be called least in the kingdom of heaven&#x27; — Cyril warns that the kingdom&#x27;s hierarchy is inverted by obedience-to-the-least; the disciple who keeps and teaches the smallest is great. Tewahedo monastic exactitude in liturgical-rubric obedience rests here.</p></aside>',
