        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Except your righteousness shall exceed the righteousness of the scribes and Pharisees&#x27; — Cyril names perissos dikaiosynē as the surplus that comes from the indwelling Spirit, not from doubled effort. The Pharisaic-righteousness floor is not &#x27;inadequate&#x27; but &#x27;incomplete&#x27; — it needs filling by Christ-given grace.</p></aside>',
