        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Swear not at all; neither by heaven, for it is God&#x27;s throne&#x27; — Cyril reads the prohibition as targeting the casual-oath culture (swearing-by-creatures-as-warrant-for-truth). The disciple&#x27;s word should not need such reinforcement. Tewahedo Sänbäte-Maryam-confraternity oath-discipline internalizes this teaching.</p></aside>',
