        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Resist not evil: but whosoever shall smite thee on thy right cheek, turn to him the other also&#x27; — Cyril reads anti-stēnai not as moral indifference to evil but as renunciation of personal vengeance; the right cheek (struck with the back of the right hand — a deliberate insult) is offered in deliberate non-escalation. Tewahedo non-retaliation discipline in monastic and lay tradition runs here.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
