        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Love your enemies, bless them that curse you&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s divine-imitation summit text. Agapate echthrous is the maximal command precisely because it requires participation in God&#x27;s own indiscriminate love; the disciple is asked to do what only the Father can do — and so the Father gives the doing.</p></aside>',
