        "d",
        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Take heed that ye do not your alms before men, to be seen of them&#x27; — Cyril reconciles Mt 6:1 with Mt 5:16: the difference is the THEATRON. Doing works to-be-seen-of-men makes men the audience and forfeits the Father&#x27;s reward; doing works that happen to be seen (with God as the intended audience) glorifies God through the visible effect.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
