        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Judge not, that ye be not judged&#x27; — Cyril carefully distinguishes krinete from diakrinete: discernment-of-truth remains required (Mt 7:6, Jn 7:24), but condemnatory-judgment of persons is reserved to the only one who sees the heart. The metrō-hō-metreite reciprocity ensures the judging-disciple gets his own standard returned.</p></aside>',
