        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Beware of false prophets, which come to you in sheep&#x27;s clothing&#x27; — Cyril marks the diagnostic challenge: pseudoprophētēs is identifiable not by claims but by fruit (the next two verses). Tewahedo discernment-of-teaching tradition (especially against Manichaean and Arian incursion in 5th-6th-c. Aksum) anchors here.</p></aside>',
