        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Many shall come from the east and from the west, and shall sit down with Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob in the kingdom of heaven&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s Gentile-mission charter. The eschatological banquet is geographically catholic by divine plan. Tewahedo missionary tradition — Frumentius&#x27;s fourth-century mission and the Nine-Saints translation arc — reads Mt 8:11 as the apostolic mandate of Ethiopian Christianization.</p></aside>',
