        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;They that be whole need not a physician, but they that are sick&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s medical-christology. The iatros (physician) image runs deep in his thought: Christ is the cosmic physician; sinners are the proper patients; the self-righteous Pharisaic &#x27;healthy&#x27; have diagnosed themselves out of medicine. Tewahedo monastic spiritual-direction tradition explicitly names the abba as iatros-tēs-psychēs (physician of the soul) on the Cyrillian model.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
