        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Whoever confesses me before men, him will I confess before my Father&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s martyr-theology pillar. Confession and denial are not psychological states but forensic realities — the eschatological court hears the earthly testimony as evidence. Tewahedo Sämā&#x27;ǝtāt (martyr-synaxarium) cycle invokes Mt 10:32-33 at every commemorating Mäzämmǝr.</p></aside>',
