        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Behold my servant, whom I have chosen; my beloved, in whom my soul is well pleased: I will put my spirit upon him&#x27; — Cyril&#x27;s Isa 42 servant-fulfillment locus. Matthew gives the longest Old-Testament citation in the Gospel here; Cyril reads the pais-mou (my servant) Christologically — the eternal Son in his incarnate servant-form. The thēsō to pneuma-mou ep&#x27;auton (I will place my Spirit upon him) names the baptismal Pentecost-foreshadowing. Tewahedo Isaiah-Lectionary uses Mt 12:18-21 as the bridge-text between Old and New Covenant readings.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
