        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The Canaanite woman: Cyril celebrates her persistent faith as the model Gentile catechumen; her self-naming &#x27;even the dogs eat of the crumbs&#x27; is humility, not abjection. Tewahedo Gentile-inclusion theology — rooted in the Ethiopian eunuch typology of Acts 8 — reads Mt 15:21-28 as one of its earliest Gospel precedents.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
