        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>STATER</strong> Greek word rendered “piece of money” (Matthew 17:27, A.V.; and “shekel” in R.V.). It was equal to two didrachmas (“tribute money,” 17:24), or four drachmas, and to about 2s. 6d. of our money. (See SHEKEL.)",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
