        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Suffer the little children to come unto me, and forbid them not, for of such is the kingdom of heaven&#x27;: Cyril cites this verse against any withholding of baptism on grounds of age. The kingdom belongs already to such as these. Tewahedo infant baptism — administered on the 40th day for boys, 80th for girls — rests squarely on this Cyrillian foundation.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
