        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>NEEDLE</strong> used only in the proverb, “to pass through a needle’s eye” (Matthew 19:24; Mark 10:25; Luke 18:25). Some interpret the expression as referring to the side gate, close to the principal gate, usually called the “eye of a needle” in the East; but it is rather to be taken literally. The Hebrew females were skilled in the use of the needle (Exodus 28:39; 26:36; Judges 5:30).",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
