        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Hosanna to the Son of David&#x27;: Cyril sees the triumphal entry as the simultaneous fulfillment of Zech 9:9 (king on a donkey) and 2 Sam 7:13 (Davidic dynasty everlasting) — the prophesied messianic king arrives in deliberately chosen humility. Tewahedo Hosaʿinnā Sunday processions, with palm-frond crosses crafted in the chancel, preserve this dual-fulfillment liturgically.</p></aside>',
