        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;God of Abraham, Isaac, and Jacob — God of the living, not of the dead&#x27;: Cyril deploys this verse against Sadducean resurrection-denial. The patriarchs live to God as the proof-text of resurrection-from-Pentateuch; the Mosaic books themselves teach the resurrection.</p></aside>',
