        "",
        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Thou shalt love the Lord thy God with all thy heart, and with all thy soul, and with all thy mind&#x27; — Cyril marks the threefold-anthropology (heart + soul + mind = kardia + psychē + dianoia) as the totality-of-personhood under the great-commandment. The agapēseis (you-shall-love) is imperative-future; love is commanded BECAUSE it is freely-willed. The Deut 6:5 Shema is fulfilled-in-Christ (the Lord-thy-God whom Israel loves IS the incarnate Word standing before them). Tewahedo catechetical-introduction (the Säwasǝw-of-Catechumens) cites Mt 22:37-40 + Deut 6:4-5 + Lev 19:18 as the entire-Torah summary.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
