        "Dictionary",
        "Easton.",
        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>TRIBE</strong> a collection of families descending from one ancestor. The “twelve tribes” of the Hebrews were the twelve collections of families which sprang from the sons of Jacob. In Matthew 24:30 the word has a wider significance. The tribes of Israel are referred to as types of the spiritual family of God (Revelation 7). (See ISRAEL, KINGDOM OF; JUDAH, KINGDOM OF.)",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
