        "comm-ethiopian",
        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;Father, if it be possible, let this cup pass from me; nevertheless not as I will, but as thou wilt&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s two-wills text. The human will of Christ recoils from suffering yet defers entirely to the Father&#x27;s saving counsel; Miaphysite Christology preserves both wills as natural to their respective natures within the one incarnate hypostasis. Tewahedo Mahǝlet (Holy Week vigil-chants) pair Mt 26:39 with Lk 22:42 as twin Gethsemane-witnesses.</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
