        "<strong>Dictionary (Easton's).</strong> <strong>POTTERS FIELD</strong> the name given to the piece of ground which was afterwards bought with the money that had been given to Judas. It was called the “field of blood” (Matthew 27:7-10). Tradition places it in the valley of Hinnom. (See ACELDAMA.)",
        "Easton's Illustrated Bible Dictionary, M. G. Easton (1897). Public domain.",
