        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>The veil of the Temple rent in twain from the top downward: Cyril sees this as the opening of the heavenly sanctuary (Heb 10:19-20). The old worship terminates at the moment the eschatological worship is inaugurated; access is granted because the High Priest has entered once-for-all by his own blood.</p></aside>',
