        "Tewahedo — Cyril of Alexandria",
        "Cyril of Alexandria (430).",
        '<aside class="note-comm-ethiopian"><strong>Cyril of Alexandria</strong> <em>Commentary on Matthew</em> <small>(c. 430 AD)</small><p>&#x27;He is not here, for he is risen, as he said&#x27;: Cyril&#x27;s resurrection-proclamation core. The empty tomb is empirical witness; the angelic proclamation is doctrinal interpretation; the two together constitute the apostolic kerygma. Tewahedo Fasika (Easter), preceded by the midnight vigil, opens with this kerygmatic announcement and the congregational response &#x27;Bä-ʾǝmma-rǝtuʿ tänśǝʾä&#x27; (&#x27;Truly he is risen&#x27;).</p></aside>',
        "Cyril of Alexandria, Commentary on Matthew (fragments), preserved in J.A. Cramer, Catenae Graecorum Patrum in Novum Testamentum, Vol. I: In Evangelia S. Matthaei et S. Marci (Oxford: University Press, 1840). PD. Greek text also in PG 72 cols. 365-474.",
